	Well, I used to be confused over this, so I decided to let others
know.  I thought that the enchanting code for weapons and armor were
identical.  WRONG!
	Weapons can be enchanted high.  Although after +5 (I think)
there is a 66% chance that you will successfully enchant it.  As for the
other 33%...*poof*.
	Armor and rings on the other hand can be enchanted to +7 at best.
When a piece of armor or ring achieves a +3 or more, then the odds of it
being destroyed are increased.  At +3, the odds of destroying it are fairly
in your favor.  At +4 with a blessed scroll of enchant armour, your odds are
more or less even.  At +5 or better, forget it.  0% chance of enchanting it
without overenchanting.

	I could still be wrong since I don't have the source lying around,
but I think this is right.

